---A `AchievementType` config contains data about one of the many achievements in the game.
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.Achievement` table:
---
---Info: A `AchievementType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot,
---however, be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Information available within an `AchievementType` includes:
---
---Prerequisites and Requirements: Achievement configs contain one or more tests, each which can be one of several
---different test types:
---
---AchievementTestSkill: Tests if skill(s) have met a certain level threshold.
---
---AchievementTestQuest: Tests if quest(s) are completed.
---
---AchievementTestAchievement: Tests if achievement(s) are completed.
---
---AchievementTestVarTotal: Tests if variable(s) have met a certain value threshold.
---
---AchievementTestVarTestBit: Test if variable bit(s) have been set to a certain value.
---
---These test types are further split into two different collections:
---
---An example would be an achievement with:
---
---This example could hide the achievement until Smithing is at level 20, revealing it only when the Player Character is
---able to craft items that meet the requirement.
---
---More information about each of the types of test is shown below.
---@class AchievementType
---@field id integer (Read-only) The ID of this config type.
---@field configName string (Read-only) The name of this config, i.e. `"CHEEVO_GODWARS_SOULSTONES"`.
---@field typeName string (Read-only) The type of this config. Will always be `"Achievement"`.
---@field name string (Read-only) The display name of this config type.
---@field reward string (Read-only) A string containing any rewards for this achievement. Multiple rewards are delimited by "<br>".
---@field isMembers boolean (Read-only) Whether this achievement is for members.
---@field category integer (Read-only) The category type of this config. Returns `-1` if none is set. Category name is available using `id.Category.FromID()`.
---@field subCategory integer (Read-only) The sub-category type of this config. Returns `-1` if none is set. Category name is available using `id.Category.FromID()`.
---@field spriteID integer (Read-only) The ID of any sprite shown for this achievement. Returns `-1` if not set.
---@field runeScore integer (Read-only) The RuneScore value of the achievement. Returns `0` if not set.
---@field hiddenType AchievementHiddenType (Read-only) The visibility behaviour of this achievement if its prerequisites are incomplete.
---@field graceExpiryRunedate integer (Read-only) The RuneDay when the grace period for this achievement expires. Before this, the achievement is always considered complete for the purpose of meta-achievements (e.g. Completion Cape). Returns -1 if not set.
---@field hasRequirementDescriptions boolean (Read-only) Whether any of the achievement requirements contains a description.
---@field totalPrereqCount integer (Read-only) How many total prerequisites this achievement contains.
---@field totalRequirementCount integer (Read-only) How many total requirements this achievement contains.
---@field dbRowConfig DBRowType? (Read-only) Any associated DBRow for this achievement. Returns `nil` if not set.
---@field tallyTarget integer (Read-only) For achievements with a tally (such as killing 100 monsters), this returns what the target value is. Each achievement can have only one tally. Returns `-1` if not set.
---@field tallyProgress integer (Read-only) For achievements with a tally, this returns the current progression count. Returns `-1` if not set.
---@field descriptions AchievementDescription[] (Read-only) Returns a list of entries, each of which contain a AchievementDescriptionType and the text for the description, i.e. [     {         "type" : AchievementDescriptionType,         "text" : "Description..."     },     ... ]
---@field prereqs AchievementTests (Read-only) Returns all prerequisites for this achievement, separated into sub-lists of requirement type, i.e. {     "skills" : [ AchievementTestSkill, ... ],     "quests" : [ AchievementTestQuest, ... ],     "achievements" : [ AchievementTestAchievement, ... ],     "varTotals" : [ AchievementTestVarTotal, ... ],     "varTestBits" : [ AchievementTestVarTestBit, ... ], }
---@field requirements AchievementTests (Read-only) Returns all requirements for this achievement, separated into sub-lists of requirement type, i.e. {     "skills" : [ AchievementTestSkill, ... ],     "quests" : [ AchievementTestQuest, ... ],     "achievements" : [ AchievementTestAchievement, ... ],     "varTotals" : [ AchievementTestVarTotal, ... ],     "varTestBits" : [ AchievementTestVarTestBit, ... ], }
---@field progress integer (Read-only) Returns a progression value for this achievement. If the value is 0 or less, then it will be a AchievementProgressType. Use `AchievementProgressType.FromID(config.progress)` to view the type name. If the value is greater than 0 then it indicates the current completion progress, where `10000` is the maximum value. For example: `local percentComplete = config.progress / 100`
---@field prereqsComplete boolean (Read-only) Whether prerequisites are regarded as completed. This is impacted by `completionCountForPrereqGroups` and GetSubItemCompletionCountForPrereqGroup() whereby not every test needs to be completed for this property to return `true`.
---@field prereqGroupCount integer (Read-only) How many separate groups of prerequisite tests exist.
---@field completionCountForPrereqGroups integer (Read-only) How many prerequisite groups need to be complete in order to consider all prerequisites as completed. For example, if `prereqGroupCount == 2` and `completionCountForPrereqGroups == 1` then only one of the two groups needs to be completed.
---@field requirementGroupCount integer (Read-only) How many separate groups of requirement tests exist.
---@field completionCountForRequirementGroups integer (Read-only) How many requirement groups need to be complete in order to consider all requirements as completed. For example, if `requirementGroupCount == 2` and `completionCountForRequirementGroups == 1` then only one of the two groups needs to be completed.
local AchievementType = {}

---Returns whether the given prerequisite group is considered complete.
---
---Depending on the value of GetSubItemCompletionCountForPrereqGroup(), this can mean all or only some of the individual
---prerequisites have actually been completed.
---@param group integer The group ID to be tested for completion. `group` is 0-indexed.
---@return boolean # Whether the prerequisite group is considered complete.
function AchievementType:GetPrereqGroupComplete(group) end

---Returns how many individual prerequisites, each with the same group, must be completed for that group to be
---considered complete.
---
---For example, if there were three prerequisites with group 0, and `GetSubItemCompletionCountForPrereqGroup(0)`
---returned a value of 1, then only one of the three prerequisites will need to be completed.
---@param group integer The group ID to be checked. `group` is 0-indexed.
---@return integer # How many items in the prerequisite group need to be completed for the entire group to be considered complete.
function AchievementType:GetSubItemCompletionCountForPrereqGroup(group) end

---Returns how many individual requirements, each with the same group, must be completed for that group to be considered
---complete.
---
---For example, if there were three requirements with group 0, and `GetSubItemCompletionCountForRequirementGroup(0)`
---returned a value of 1, then only one of the three requirements will need to be completed.
---@param group integer The group ID to be checked. `group` is 0-indexed.
---@return integer # How many items in the requirement group need to be completed for the entire group to be considered complete.
function AchievementType:GetSubItemCompletionCountForRequirementGroup(group) end

---This test collects Player Character's levels in the given SkillTypes into one cumulative total, and compares it
---against the target total level.
---
---Typically this test will contain only one skill, but is able to support more.
---
---Info: All properties are read-only.
---@class AchievementTestSkill
---@field group integer (Read-only) The group ID of this test.
---@field skillTypes SkillType[] (Read-only) All skill types to be tested. The levels of each skill type are added together.
---@field totalLevels integer (Read-only) The target total skill levels which must be achieved.
---@field description string (Read-only) The description for this test, if supplied.
---@field isComplete boolean (Read-only) Whether the Player Character has completed this test.

---This test checks whether the Player Character has completed the given quest.
---
---Info: All properties are read-only.
---@class AchievementTestQuest
---@field group integer (Read-only) The group ID of this test.
---@field quest QuestTypeConfig (Read-only) The quest config to test for completion.
---@field description string (Read-only) The description for this test, if supplied.
---@field isComplete boolean (Read-only) Whether the Player Character has completed this test.

---This test checks whether the Player Character has completed the given achievement.
---
---Info: All properties are read-only.
---@class AchievementTestAchievement
---@field group integer (Read-only) The group ID of this test.
---@field achievement AchievementType (Read-only) The achievement config to test for completion.
---@field description string (Read-only) The description for this test, if supplied.
---@field isComplete boolean (Read-only) Whether the Player Character has completed this test.

---This test checks whether the cumulative total of a given list of VarPlayers values meets or exceeds a given total
---value.
---
---An example would be a test for '50 bosses killed' that accumulates the values of many separate VarPlayers which
---individually track kills for a specific boss.
---
---A more basic example would be '20 oak logs chopped' where only one VarPlayer value is compared to the total.
---
---Info: All properties are read-only.
---@class AchievementTestVarTotal
---@field group integer (Read-only) The group ID of this test.
---@field vars VarType[] (Read-only) The list of VarPlayer variables to accumulate the values of.
---@field totalValue integer (Read-only) The target value which must be met or exceeded.
---@field description string (Read-only) The description for this test, if supplied.
---@field isComplete boolean (Read-only) Whether the Player Character has completed this test.

---This test checks whether a specific bit in a VarPlayer value matches a given value of `0` or `1`.
---
---Info: All properties are read-only.
---@class AchievementTestVarTestBit
---@field group integer (Read-only) The group ID of this test.
---@field var VarType (Read-only) The VarPlayer variable holding the value which is tested.
---@field bitIndex integer (Read-only) The bit index of the tested value. bitIndex is 0-indexed.
---@field bitValue integer (Read-only) The target value which must be matched. This is typically always `1`.
---@field description string (Read-only) The description for this test, if supplied.
---@field isComplete boolean (Read-only) Whether the Player Character has completed this test.

---The tests of an achievement's prerequisites or requirements, a list for each kind of test.
---@class AchievementTests
---@field skills AchievementTestSkill[]? (Read-only) The tests of skill levels.
---@field quests AchievementTestQuest[]? (Read-only) The tests of completed quests.
---@field achievements AchievementTestAchievement[]? (Read-only) The tests of completed achievements.
---@field varTotals AchievementTestVarTotal[]? (Read-only) The tests of variables' totals.
---@field varTestBits AchievementTestVarTestBit[]? (Read-only) The tests of variable bits.

---One of an achievement's descriptions, for a game mode.
---@class AchievementDescription
---@field type AchievementDescriptionType (Read-only) The kind of description this is.
---@field text string (Read-only) The description's text.

---Achievement progress is provided by the `AchievementType.progress` property.
---
---A positive value indicates that the achievement has partial completion, while a 0 or negative value indicates one of
---the enumerations below.
---@enum AchievementProgressType
AchievementProgressType = {
    READY = 0,
    LOCKED = -1,
    COMPLETE = -2,
    GRACE = -3,
    DEPRECATED = -4,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `AchievementProgressType.FromID(AchievementProgressType.READY)` is `"READY"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function AchievementProgressType.FromID(value) end

---Alternate achievement descriptions are available for various game modes.
---
---These types are provided along with the relevant string by the `AcheivementType.descriptions` property.
---@enum AchievementDescriptionType
AchievementDescriptionType = {
    DEFAULT = 0,
    IRONMAN = 1,
    GROUP_IRONMAN_SIZE_2 = 2,
    GROUP_IRONMAN_SIZE_3 = 3,
    GROUP_IRONMAN_SIZE_4 = 4,
    GROUP_IRONMAN_SIZE_5 = 5,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `AchievementDescriptionType.FromID(AchievementDescriptionType.DEFAULT)` is `"DEFAULT"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function AchievementDescriptionType.FromID(value) end

---An achievement's display behaviour is controlled by this enumeration, and is provided by the
---`AchievementType.hiddenType` property.
---@enum AchievementHiddenType
AchievementHiddenType = {
    ---Achievement is always displayed
    NEVER = 0,
    ---Achievement is hidden if any prerequisites are incomplete.
    IF_LOCKED = 1,
    ---Achievement is hidden until all requirements are completed.
    UNTIL_COMPLETE = 2,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `AchievementHiddenType.FromID(AchievementHiddenType.NEVER)` is `"NEVER"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function AchievementHiddenType.FromID(value) end
